WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
You sort of see sales in everything and

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.320
everywhere. So, what are some ways that

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.760
you can practice in order to work your

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.680
way up to the point where you're asking

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.280
you know, individuals for $500,000

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.760
checks for a a deal that you have

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.960
working on.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.520
>> I I had a I had a wake-up a

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.240
come-to-Jesus moment with a mentor at

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.320
Ithaca, New York. His name's Dan Cohen.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.840
Um he had sold a foundation repair

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.240
business for almost $10 million and he

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.800
was, you know, a a

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.720
a fellow of entrepreneurship at Cornell

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.440
at the time and I asked him to get

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.520
breakfast and I had just started a

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.480
business and I was a big-time

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.400
entrepreneur and I had big dreams and

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.760
big goals and we sit down for breakfast

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.640
and he says, "Nick,

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.680
do you consider yourself to be good at

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.000
sales and do you like sales?"

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.440
This is the first question. No, "How are

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.080
you?" No, "What are you going to order?"

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.440
That's the first thing he said.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.080
And I could sense that I was supposed to

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.320
say I liked sales, but I was honest and

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.720
I said,

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.480
"Um no, I

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.360
I get really uncomfortable in sales. I

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.560
don't like it. It's not for me. I'm more

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.760
of a operator and innovator. I picture

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.280
myself at the whiteboard making

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.000
decisions. Like

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.840
I'm going to make marketing decisions

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.200
and I just spewed a bunch of bullshit."

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.320
And he looks at me and he goes, "Nick,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.000
if you don't like sales, you need to go

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.000
get a job."

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.000
And I was like, "Whoa." Hit me like a

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.000
ton of bricks. I was like

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.400
it shook me to my core.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.360
He's like, "Every part of life is sales.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.160
Every part of business is sales. You're

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:26.160
convincing you're selling your employees

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.640
on trusting you with their career.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.040
You're selling your employees on doing

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.080
what you need them to do when they join

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.000
your company. You're selling your

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.000
vendors on selling to you. You're

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.840
selling investors on investing with you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.720
and you of course you're selling

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.160
customers on buying from you.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.960
That is your job as an entrepreneur 100%

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.080
of the time is to sell you yourself and

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.200
your ideas to everybody around you.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.766
So, if you don't like it,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.240
get a go go get a job.

00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:48.680
>> [laughter]

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.440
>> But then he told me the good news. He

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.600
told me the good news that you could

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.560
practice it and you can turn yourself

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.200
into a great sales person.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.040
Um so,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.160
it's the

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.560
I I have a lot of very tactical tips on

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.200
sales in that book. I have a whole

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.840
chapter about the framework I use to

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.520
sell to how to build trust to, you know,

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.726
how to flip the script and how some how

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.039
some have somebody help,

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:10.080
>> [gasps]

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:11.480
>> you know, sell themselves on you once

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.800
you once you built that trust and told

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.280
them what you can do.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.640
But unfortunately, like sales is a

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.320
muscle.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.840
You can't you got to go to the gym and

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.160
lift the weights. You got to practice

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.680
and you got to just turn the mindset.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.240
Because I was just

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.120
Okay, I was a little bit extroverted,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.880
but I was really uncomfortable in every

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.760
single sales environment.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.080
But I pounded it into myself and

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.200
practiced to to become a good

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.880
salesperson. Anybody can do it. So, go

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.920
to the gym and lift the weights.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.920
>> Yeah.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.440
So, my my favorite tactic that you

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.440
mentioned and I mean it's it's not a

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.560
mind trick. It's not a manipulation, but

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:50.000
it is incredibly powerful and in the

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:51.680
sales situations that I've been in

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.120
by virtue of just asking questions

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.240
instead of trying to be the the person

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.520
giving the information and trying to,

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:02.400
you know, basically convince people to

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:04.239
do something and showing like just real

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.560
care for what the other person's trying

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:08.440
to accomplish and then

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.040
pair that with giving people options of

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.840
ways that they can engage with me and my

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:15.600
business like was just a huge like

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.280
mindset unlock that that changed

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.320
everything for for how that worked for

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.519
me. And the question where you kind of

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.400
turn it on people and you just say,

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:23.920
well,

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.720
you know, you kind of outline the the

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.880
pitfalls and you're like,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.760
How is it you you think

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.280
why am I a good fit for you?

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.320
Right? I think it's just a an incredible

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.640
way to get people thinking in a

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.760
different way and

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.640
I'm curious

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:40.720
unpack that a little bit for us and and

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.480
are there any other types of of

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.760
questions or ways that you encounter

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.400
people that tend to bring unexpected

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.239
results?

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.040
>> Yeah, look, my main goal when I go into

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:50.880
every single sales interaction is to add

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.280
value to somebody's life.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.240
And if they feel like they're going to

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.320
step away from our interaction knowing

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.160
something or having value added

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.320
or being smarter or being more aware of

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.400
a potential problem or whatever it might

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.400
be,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:06.000
they're going to build trust with me.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.400
So, if I can build that trust

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.920
by, you know, speaking the language,

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.640
talking about the downfalls, talking

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.760
about um you know, showing them that I

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.120
care and adding value to them,

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.079
then I like to talk about the downfalls.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.320
My next step is like, "Hey, look, like

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:20.480
if I'm selling investors on a deal, like

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.000
this could go bad. Like the the interest

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.800
rates could go up. Like this is a this

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.360
is a different ballgame. Like what makes

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.560
you think like this is our situation. We

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.600
could be stuck in this for a really long

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.600
time.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.040
We could miss projections. Like And then

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.120
I flip the script right then. Like right

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.280
after talking about these downsides,

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.600
I'll be like,

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.160
"So, Craig, like what makes you think

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.440
that this is a good investment? Like why

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.400
do you like storage or why do you like

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.520
this business? And what makes you think

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.440
that we'd be a good fit?"

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.760
And then I'd be quiet.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.040
And something amazing happens a lot of

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.600
the time.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.120
When some A, you reset expectations so

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.560
that it's not a super stressful

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.160
relationship and they don't have

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.880
unreasonable expectations of you. And if

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.400
they do, they will weed themselves out.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.680
And it's great.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.160
But more often than not,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.320
they start to sell themselves on you.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.960
They want to work with somebody like

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.360
that that's going to add value, talk

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.760
about the risks, like be realistic.

